meridian oss
============

build:  make
run:    make run          (rebuilds meridian.db from data/)
check:  make check        (billing rule checks, bin/billing-test)
reg:    make register     (invoice register for 2026-07)
demo:   make demo         (invoice-api :8082 + dashboard pages on :8083)

binaries land in bin/

  mediation      nightly ingest, writes meridian.db
  inventory-api  :8081   /sites  /circuits  /capacity
  billing-run    monthly invoice register, --json for the reconciliation feed
  billing-test   billing rule checks
  invoice-api    :8082   /invoices?acct=...&period=...
  ipam           management address report (10.20.0.0/16)

dashboard/index.html and dashboard/billing.html are static pages, open them in
a browser with inventory-api and invoice-api running.

dashboard/capacity.html is the sales desk capacity check. it asks
/capacity?requested=<mbps> and shows what is left at each customer location.
available = total - allocated, we do not hold back a maintenance buffer.
serviceable locations come from data/locations.csv.

data/ holds the telemetry drops. billing/accounts/ is the account master.

the billing rules all live in billing/rules/telco_rules.c and go through
billing/invoice.cpp:

  rating          whole gigabytes, partial gigs round up, $10 a gig over plan
  proration       30 day billing month, mid cycle plan changes split on it
  promo           promo credits expire at the end of the cycle they were issued
  suspension      a suspended line is billed the full month, no credit
  lines           3-9 lines 5% off recurring, 10+ lines 10%
  latefee         10 day grace after the due date, then 1.5% of the balance
  tax             GST/HST on the pre discount amount, PST/QST on what is paid
  discounts       loyalty credit off the subtotal

that file is plain C because vantage-telco vendors it and calls the compiled
object through ctypes: both estates bill from one implementation. it is the
only place these rules may be written. billing/rules/RULES.md has the rest,
including the cases still waiting on a finance decision.

make vectors regenerates billing/rules/conformance_vectors.json, the shared
contract the vantage java report module is tested against. make check fails
if the checked in copy is stale.

the provinces we bill are BC, AB, ON and QC. the province is on the account
record (PROVINCE=) and on the invoice register page.

tools/parity in vantage-telco runs both registers off the same usage feed and
prints any difference; it should print none.

contacts: ops-eng (pager), billing questions -> finance
